# Ignore everything at the repository root by default, then re-include what an image build needs.
#
# The exclusion uses a single star, not two, on purpose.
#
# A ** pattern prunes whole directories (like cmd/) before their files are evaluated, so a later re-include of the files inside them never takes effect and the build context ends up without any source.
*

# Keep the Go module files so the dependency layer can be cached.
!go.mod
!go.sum

# Keep the Go source trees the binaries build from.
!cmd
!api
!internal

# Drop test files from the kept trees, since images never run them.
**/*_test.go
